  "body": "### What problem are you trying to solve?\n\nNostr is a decentralized social network. Think of it as IRC but for \"notes and other stuff\".\r\nIn nostr, users are identified by their public key, and they can use different clients to interact with the protocol.\r\n\r\nThere's an annoying inconvenience: if I share a link to my profile, I'm already including a specific client, that may not be your preferred client ([example](https://primal.net/p/npub13c3efljydkv60vhnwjyxj7ptryeqjzx3wxm26l7gfe68zpheh32qpwnsz3))\r\n\r\nTo solve this, there's a Nostr Improvement Proposal (NIP) that defines the `nostr:` scheme: [NIP-21](https://nips.nostr.com/21)\n\n### What solutions exist today?\n\n* Link with client specific\n\n### How would you solve it?\n\nby adding `nostr` to the `registerProtocolHandler`, but not as custom handler, no web+ prefix\n\n### Anything else?\n\n_No response_",
